10. DAX Design Principles

The project follows these principles:

1. Reusable Measures

Business calculations are created as reusable measures rather than repeatedly calculated inside individual visuals.

2. Filter-Aware Analysis

Measures respond dynamically to Power BI slicers and dimensions such as:

Plan
Region
Industry
Customer Segment
Trial Status
Date
Feature
Support Priority
3. Safe Ratio Calculations

DIVIDE() is used for percentage and ratio calculations to avoid division-by-zero errors.

4. Business-Oriented KPIs

Measures are designed around business questions rather than technical calculations alone.

11. Business Value of the DAX Layer

The DAX layer converts the Gold data model into a decision-support layer.

Gold Data Model
      ↓
DAX Measures
      ↓
Business KPIs
      ↓
Interactive Power BI
      ↓
Business Decisions

The measures allow management to evaluate:

Revenue performance
Customer retention
Subscription movement
Product engagement
Product quality
Customer support performance

12. Important Note

DAX measures should always be validated against the final Power BI semantic model before deployment.

The formulas documented here describe the intended KPI logic and should match the final measure definitions used in the .pbix file.
